<Layout title="Selected work — Mario Marcolongo"><SiteNav/><main id="main-content" class="presence-shell"><p class="eyebrow">Selected work</p><h1>Research, tools &amp; contributions.</h1><p class="lede">Scientific source work, practical tools and accepted open-source contributions.</p><p>{P.authorship}</p><div class="project-gallery">{P.projects.filter(project=>!['telegram'].includes(project.id)).map(project=><WorkRow project={project}/>)}</div><section class="presence-section"><h2>Further experience &amp; contributions</h2><p><a href="/experience">Full experience and responsibilities</a> brings together paid work, volunteer research support and independent contributions.</p><p><a href="/work/wikimedia">Wikipedia, Wikidata &amp; Wikimedia Commons</a>: sustained source review, structured-data work and scientific communication.</p><p><a href="/work/atlas">AI Safety Formalization Atlas</a>: five merged contributions to source auditing, citation provenance and repository tooling, plus a September 2026 draft coauthorship.</p><p><a href="/work/telegram">Telegram and cloud automation</a> documents a practical workflow and its architecture. <a href="/research-operations">Qualitative research support</a> describes a scoped volunteer contribution in a University of Padua project.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/mariomarcolongo/Questionnaire-of-Cognitive-and-Affective-Empathy-QCAE-online-questionnaire">QCAE questionnaire implementation</a> makes an existing instrument available online. It does not establish a new instrument or independent psychometric validation.</p><p><a href="https://mariomarcolongo.github.io/emergent-humanity/">Emergent Humanity</a> is an independent interactive narrative and network simulation: concept and interaction design with AI-assisted implementation.</p></section></main><SiteFooter/></Layout>
